 seat a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D", "Prediction markets price Bennett near 88-89% to win", "Incumbent Kean carries a slight incumbency penalty in a favorable Democratic midterm environment", "Bennett has kept pace financially with outside support, while Kean holds a cash-on-hand edge"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Democratic edge of roughly six points: an even-PVI district in a strong midterm environment, an incumbent rated a flip by every major rater, and a September poll showing Bennett up five. Markets price the race somewhat stronger for Democrats than the polling alone, supporting a Likely D call with meaningful residual uncertainty.", "watch": "A late shift in the national environment or a strong debate-driven rebound for Kean could pull this back toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Thomas Kean Jr. (R) is running."]}, "overview": "New Jersey's 7th District is an even-PVI swing seat where first-term Republican incumbent Tom Kean Jr. faces Democrat Rebecca Bennett. Every major expert rating, from Tilt D to Likely D, calls the seat a Democratic flip, and prediction markets give Bennett roughly an 88-89% chance of winning. A September live-caller poll of likely voters showed Bennett ahead by five points, consistent with a fundamentals picture that combines a favorable midterm environment with a modest incumbency drag on Kean.\n\nBennett has raised over $4.2 million with outside groups supporting her, while Kean has raised slightly more and holds a large cash-on-hand advantage. Recent debates over Iran, tariffs, and affordability have kept the race competitive, but the weight of ratings, markets, and polling points to a Democratic edge of about six points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "